llity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=A+4I.$\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that if $\\lambda =4$ is an eigenvalue of $A,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(A+4I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $A.$ As a result, the matrix $M=A+4I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. Since $M=A+4I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(A+4I)\\ne {R}^{2},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A+4I)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371521 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371522 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371523 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371524 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371525 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1041 "selection" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371523 13194139535871 true] [17592186371520 1110 #uuid "9b8ee5ed-b197-594c-b314-3788470536d2" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371521 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371521 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371521 1111 #uuid "f8d594c9-4229-5730-9c8f-fbb4a53c61ed" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371522 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371522 1111 #uuid "a08f0cc8-15b8-52c4-ba43-fd8807e9f29e" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371523 1034 "I only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371523 1111 #uuid "3616b771-3d73-5a91-ad7d-8b3833d5cd6c" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371524 1034 "III only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371524 1111 #uuid "c6f35db3-fdb7-5a72-aad1-b01f8bd1241f" 13194139535871 true] [17592186