90f-a9ba7a3808c9" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371533 1145 "Since $B$ is invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, $0$ can't be an eigenvalue of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =0$ should not be a solution to the corresponding characteristic equation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given equations in turn.\n\n- Equation I could  be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation II could be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation III **cannot** be the characteristic equation of $B$ since $\\lambda =0$ is a root of the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371535 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371536 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371537 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371538 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371539 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1041 "selection" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371539 13194139535871 true] [17592186371534 1110 #uuid "f0aaaa32-1e93-52d5-8e83-de8cedd7b788" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371535 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371535 1111 #uuid "0698cac2-a4c0-5506-85f7-698a05b12465" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371536 1034 "None of the listed" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371536 1111 #uuid "d64553e5-6b51-547d-8757-29ef471e62d9" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371537 1034 "I only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371537 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371537 1111 #uuid "7b2734c8-4d9a-58fa-9a27-01ace5ab128a" 13194139535871 true] [1759218637153