(C+3I)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(C+3I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $C-3I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that if $M=C+3I$ is singular, then $(C+3I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $C.$ As a result, $\\lambda =-3$ is an eigenvalue of $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371591 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371592 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371593 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371594 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371595 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1041 "selection" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371591 13194139535871 true] [17592186371590 1110 #uuid "ae6ae590-ed86-508c-9580-ee7ab020421e" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371591 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371591 1111 #uuid "fb57f54d-3d0f-5e5a-8367-217cd86e939e" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371592 1034 "I only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371592 1111 #uuid "61534bda-90c3-5674-bc41-ba018a3cfecc" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371593 1034 "III only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371593 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371593 1111 #uuid "d644d173-15e6-5bcf-ab03-3ecd9f17cc0a" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371594 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371594 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371594 1111 #uuid "5ca2946a-39c2-50d9-b79d-9738c3161e1e" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371595 1034 "II only" 13194139535871 true] [17592186371595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535871 true] [17592186371595 11